  "backstory": {
    "opening": [
      "{name} was born in {home}, {years} years ago, in a hard {season} that people there still remember.",
      "{name} grew up in {home}, the {nth} child of a family with more mouths than bread.",
      "{name} was raised in {home}, among {culture} folk who expected little of the world and got less.",
      "{name} came into the world in {home} in the {season} of a bad year, and was not expected to see the next.",
      "Ask in {home} and someone will remember {name}: the {nth} of a brood, always somewhere {pronoun} should not be.",
      "{name} was {years} years in {home} before the road. Most of them were cold, and some were hungry.",
      "In {home}, where {culture} folk bury their dead facing the hills, {name} was born the {nth} of many.",
      "{name}'s first memory is of {home} in {season}: smoke, mud, and a voice calling {object} in for supper."
    ],
    "middle": [
      "{background_line}",
      "{background_line} It left marks that have not faded.",
      "{background_line} {turn}",
      "{turn} {background_line}"
    ],
    "turn": [
      "A fever took {possessive} mother the winter {pronoun} turned twelve.",
      "There was a debt, and then there was no house.",
      "A brother went to the wars and did not come back; nobody would say how.",
      "Once, a stranger at the inn told {object} the world was wider than {home}, and {pronoun} never forgot it.",
      "There was a girl, or a boy, or a promise, and none of it came to anything.",
      "A flood took the lower fields and half the village with them.",
      "{pronoun_cap} saw a man hanged at the crossroads and did not sleep for a week.",
      "Somebody {pronoun} trusted sold {object} out for a handful of silver.",
      "Raiders came one harvest, and after that {pronoun} kept a knife under {possessive} pillow."
    ],
    "closing": [
      "Now {pronoun} is on the road, with {coin} in {possessive} purse and no one to answer to.",
      "{pronoun_cap} left with a pack, a grudge and a reason not to look back.",
      "Whatever {pronoun} was, the road does not care; it only asks whether {pronoun} can keep walking.",
      "One morning {pronoun} simply went, and the door of {home} has stayed shut behind {object} since.",
      "{pronoun_cap} owes nobody anything now, and nobody owes {object}, which is a kind of freedom.",
      "What {pronoun} is looking for, {pronoun} could not tell you. {pronoun_cap} will know it when {pronoun} sees it.",
      "The road was the only thing that ever asked nothing of {object}, so {pronoun} took it.",
      "{pronoun_cap} has {coin} and a name nobody knows yet. Both can change."
    ]
  },
  "background_lines": {
    "soldier": [
      "Years in the ranks taught {object} to march, to dig, and to keep quiet when officers argued over the dead.",
      "{name} served a lord who paid late and fought often, and came out of it with a limp and a habit of counting exits.",
      "Two campaigns and a siege taught {object} that glory is a word for people who were somewhere else."
    ],
    "acolyte": [
      "The temple fed and clothed {object}, and taught {object} its prayers and which of its priests to fear.",
      "{name} swept the temple floors for years before anyone let {object} near the altar, and learned more from the floors.",
      "Raised on psalms and thin soup, {name} knows the rites by heart and has doubts {pronoun} tells nobody."
    ],
    "criminal": [
      "Cold nights and quick hands taught {object} a trade the watch would hang {object} for.",
      "{name} ran with a gang that sold anything that was not nailed down, and some things that were.",
      "There is a town where {name}'s face is on a notice by the gate, badly drawn, which is the only luck {pronoun} has had."
    ],
    "folk_hero": [
      "When trouble came to the village it was {name} who stood up, and the village has never let {object} forget it.",
      "{name} once stood alone in a lane between the village and a band of thieves, and the thieves turned back.",
      "The villagers still tell how {name} faced down a lord's bailiff, though the story grows every time."
    ],
    "noble": [
      "Born to a name and land, {name} learned manners, swordplay and the thousand small cruelties of a great house.",
      "{name} is the younger child of a house with more pride than silver, and was always going to have to make {possessive} own way.",
      "A house feud, an inheritance, a cousin with a better lawyer: {name} kept the name and lost the land."
    ],
    "sage": [
      "Long years among books gave {object} learning, bad eyesight and a head full of unanswered questions.",
      "{name} copied other men's books by candlelight until {pronoun} began to disagree with them.",
      "A scholar's apprentice, {name} learned seven dead tongues and not one useful one."
    ],
    "outlander": [
      "The wild country taught {object} to track, to hunt and to go days without speaking to another soul.",
      "{name} grew up beyond the last farms, where the wolves are bolder than the people and the winters longer than both.",
      "Herding beasts on the high pastures, {name} learned the weather, the stars and the silence."
    ],
    "guild_artisan": [
      "A guild master's beatings and a long apprenticeship made {object} good at a trade that pays badly.",
      "{name} learned a craft from a master who drank, and finished the master's work for years without the credit.",
      "Seven years of apprenticeship, a guild mark, and a workshop that burned down the month {pronoun} opened it."
    ]
  },
